<Window x:Class="EQBuddy.QuestsWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="EQBuddy Quest Tracker" SizeToContent="Height"
        WindowStyle="None" AllowsTransparency="True" Background="Transparent"
        Topmost="True" ShowInTaskbar="False" ResizeMode="CanResize"
        Width="880" WindowStartupLocation="Manual">
    <!-- A THIN HOST since E-3 Phase 2 PR 3. Everything a reader used to find here is in
         QuestsView.xaml, lifted so the Evolved shell can hold the same surface without
         holding a window — the same split World PR 1 made for SpawnsView, and the reason
         is the same: there is no clean chrome/content seam in a borderless hand-drawn
         window, so the WHOLE bordered panel went across and what stayed is only what a
         literal OS window owns.

         Nothing about the arrangement changed. **There is no element here at all**, on
         purpose: the view is assigned as `Content` in the constructor, so the tree is
         Window → QuestsView exactly as it was Window → Border before. A wrapper would be
         one more layout level than the shell's room has, and `WindowZoom` puts its
         LayoutTransform on `window.Content` — which must be the thing that scales. -->
</Window>
